# Danse macabre, the main theme
# Composer: Camille Saint-Saens (1835-1921). Work: Danse macabre, Op. 40 (1874), public domain.
# Arrangement: ours, for four chip voices, 2026-10-25. Written from the score's own material: the harp's twelve
# strokes of midnight on D, the solo violin's tuning on A and E-flat (the tritone) and G and D, and the flute's main
# waltz theme as printed in its published incipit (Mouvement modere de Valse, 3/4, G minor; the public-domain
# thematic catalogue "Orchesterwerke Romantik Themen" on Wikimedia Commons, page 684). That incipit ends after
# nine bars: the four-bar answer, the waltz chords, the xylophone break and the close are ours.
# One row is an eighth note (tempo 180: quarter = 180, one 3/4 bar a second).
# Columns: lead (pulse 25%) | harmony (pulse 50%) | bass (triangle) | drums (noise). Tokens as in fox_run.tune.
vol 11 6 13 8
tempo 180
